<p>
<code>worldgen/treengenproperties.json</code> lists every tree/shrub generator as a climate band
(temperature/rain/fertility/forest-density range, each stored 0-255 and normalized to 0-1 here).
Each generator's own <code>worldgen/treegen/&lt;Generator&gt;.json</code> file is read just for
its log/leaves block codes, and saplings are matched back to their generator via the sapling
block's own glob-keyed <code>attributes.treeGenByType</code> -- this is how a species climate band
ends up cross-linked to the concrete sapling/log/leaves block codes that actually show up on
those blocks' own item pages.
</p>
